A helper returns the largest element of an array. It must work for both `int[]` and `string[]` and use no casts. It must also pass `best` to `CompareTo` as a `T`, so an `int` argument is not boxed. Fill in the smallest constraint that makes the body compile:

```csharp
static T Largest<T>(T[] items) where T : {{constraint}}
{
    T best = items[0];
    foreach (var item in items)
        if (item.CompareTo(best) > 0) best = item;
    return best;
}
```

A message bus offers two versions of a registration method. `IHandler` is an interface with a `Handle()` method.

```csharp
// A
static void Register(object handler)
{
    var h = (IHandler)handler;   // explicit cast
    h.Handle();
}

// B
static void Register<T>(T handler) where T : IHandler
{
    handler.Handle();
}
```

A caller passes an instance of `AuditLog`, a class that does **not** implement `IHandler`, to each version. For each version, state whether the mistake is caught at compile time or at run time, and what happens.
